1
00:00:00,567 --> 00:00:01,733
<i> This Golda Briones,</i>

2
00:00:01,867 --> 00:00:04,467
<i>how sure are you that she's not
an asset for the enemy?</i>

3
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:07,100
<i> 15 million pesos in one year.</i>

4
00:00:07,233 --> 00:00:08,567
<i> His rank is Major.</i>

5
00:00:08,700 --> 00:00:11,533
<i>Even a full colonel won't make
that money in ten years.</i>

6
00:00:11,667 --> 00:00:14,267
<i>If I get suspended,
I can accept it.</i>

7
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:15,567
<i> I don't care what they say.</i>

8
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:18,033
<i>But if my own family
abandons me...</i>

9
00:00:18,167 --> 00:00:20,467
<i>There's a CCTV that doesn't
belong to the village.</i>

10
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:21,900
<i> They didn't clean it up.</i>

11
00:00:22,033 --> 00:00:23,100
<i> So it's a she.</i>

12
00:00:23,233 --> 00:00:25,200
<i> We're looking for a woman.</i>

13
00:00:25,333 --> 00:00:26,233
<i> That's what suits you</i>

14
00:00:26,367 --> 00:00:27,767
<i>with all your slandering
of Major Delgado!</i>

15
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:29,767
<i> Dizon's exposé didn't help.</i>

16
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:32,033
<i>You are placed under preventive
suspension.</i>

17
00:00:32,167 --> 00:00:33,400
<i> Pending full investigation.</i>

18
00:00:33,533 --> 00:00:36,133
<i>It's easy for you to say
that my father is a bad person.</i>

19
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:38,900
<i>You don't care about the lives
of the people you're slandering!</i>

20
00:00:39,033 --> 00:00:40,667
<i> You only think about yourself!</i>

21
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,633
You're so mean, Joey!
Why did you do that?

22
00:01:01,767 --> 00:01:02,767
You're so brave!

23
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:04,967
I'm not afraid of him.

24
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:06,400
Even if he sues you?

25
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:07,767
Yes.

26
00:01:08,067 --> 00:01:09,500
I won't back down from him.

27
00:01:10,267 --> 00:01:11,600
Okay...

28
00:01:13,367 --> 00:01:14,300
Uncle.

29
00:01:14,433 --> 00:01:15,200
Peter.

30
00:01:15,333 --> 00:01:16,400
It's good that you're here.

31
00:01:16,533 --> 00:01:18,067
There's a new delivery of wires.

32
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:19,600
Make an inventory
in the stockroom.

33
00:01:19,733 --> 00:01:20,667
Okay, Uncle.

34
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:27,967
You know, if that Andrew
sues you,

35
00:01:28,100 --> 00:01:30,000
Aunt Clarissa will have even
more problems.

36
00:01:31,167 --> 00:01:33,733
I was just defending my father.

37
00:01:34,100 --> 00:01:36,867
He doesn't deserve
to be bashed online.

38
00:01:44,233 --> 00:01:45,500
Good morning.

39
00:01:47,300 --> 00:01:48,867
Are you the owner here?

40
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:51,300
Yes, it's me.
What can I do for you?

41
00:01:51,433 --> 00:01:55,233
Are you the ones who installed
the CCTV in District One?

42
00:01:56,767 --> 00:01:58,533
Yes, it's us. Why?

43
00:02:02,467 --> 00:02:05,667
We need to recover some
recorded video.

44
00:02:05,933 --> 00:02:07,700
But someone said one of your
employee already went

45
00:02:07,833 --> 00:02:09,600
to update it, so it was deleted.

46
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:15,200
<i>Who is that?
Is there someone there?</i>

47
00:02:20,533 --> 00:02:22,300
What are you doing there?

48
00:02:22,433 --> 00:02:25,433
Peter, one of the guys outside,

49
00:02:25,567 --> 00:02:28,333
is among those who I took
the video of in the alley.

50
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:32,200
Peter, come here first.

51
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:36,633
Just stay here.

52
00:02:43,367 --> 00:02:44,200
Yes?

53
00:02:45,633 --> 00:02:46,400
Uncle?

54
00:02:46,533 --> 00:02:48,300
Who updated the system
in District One?

55
00:02:48,467 --> 00:02:49,800
Is it scheduled?

56
00:02:56,200 --> 00:02:58,533
What? Do you know anything
about the system update

57
00:02:58,667 --> 00:02:59,800
they're talking about?

58
00:03:02,233 --> 00:03:03,767
No, I don't know.

59
00:03:03,900 --> 00:03:07,967
I'm sure it wasn't me,
so I don't know.

60
00:03:09,267 --> 00:03:12,067
Sir, I'll check with my other
staff first, okay?

61
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:13,933
Maybe they updated it.

62
00:03:14,067 --> 00:03:16,433
But in the logbook,
it's not yet scheduled.

63
00:03:16,567 --> 00:03:18,833
Do you have a female staff
member here?

64
00:03:18,967 --> 00:03:20,667
We're looking for someone.

65
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:23,167
A woman? Yes, there is.

66
00:03:24,833 --> 00:03:26,833
That's Precious, my secretary.

67
00:03:26,967 --> 00:03:28,367
Is it her that
you're looking for?

68
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:32,767
No.

69
00:03:33,467 --> 00:03:35,400
Gentlemen, do you need
anything else?

70
00:03:35,533 --> 00:03:37,833
We're a bit busy.

71
00:03:37,967 --> 00:03:42,200
- Nothing more. Thank you.
- Thank you. Okay.

72
00:03:43,733 --> 00:03:44,933
That girl is driving me crazy.

73
00:03:45,067 --> 00:03:47,367
What? Do you want to sue her
for trespassing?

74
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:48,367
Assault?

75
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:49,967
We have footage here.

76
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:52,333
We have a recording
of what she did.

77
00:03:52,467 --> 00:03:53,767
No, no need. Let's not make
a big deal out of it.

78
00:03:58,467 --> 00:04:01,667
<i>It's easy for you to say
that my father is a bad person!</i>

79
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:04,200
<i>Because you hate the police!
You're the one who's biased!</i>

80
00:04:04,333 --> 00:04:07,433
<i>You don't care about the lives
of the people you're ruining.</i>

81
00:04:07,567 --> 00:04:08,833
<i> You're smart.</i>

82
00:04:08,967 --> 00:04:12,833
<i>But that's all you have.
Brains but no heart!</i>

83
00:04:15,433 --> 00:04:17,100
Wait, where are you going?

84
00:04:17,233 --> 00:04:19,133
Aren't we going to finish
the recording?

85
00:04:19,267 --> 00:04:21,533
Well, we're almost done
cleaning up here.

86
00:04:23,367 --> 00:04:24,500
Let's call it a day.

87
00:04:39,333 --> 00:04:40,133
Peter.

88
00:04:43,433 --> 00:04:45,200
Are you sure the footage
where I was captured

89
00:04:45,333 --> 00:04:46,367
is no longer in the system?

90
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:47,067
Yes.

91
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:48,333
I deleted it all.

92
00:04:48,467 --> 00:04:52,033
On the main drive, in the bin,
in the recycle bin. Everything!

93
00:04:52,167 --> 00:04:54,000
Even an IT expert can't find
anything there.

94
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:56,867
So I don't have to worry.

95
00:04:58,900 --> 00:05:02,433
But why did they ask your uncle
if he had a female employee?

96
00:05:03,933 --> 00:05:07,233
That means they knew they
had to find a female.

97
00:05:08,700 --> 00:05:09,733
It seems that way.

98
00:05:10,033 --> 00:05:10,900
But how?

99
00:05:11,933 --> 00:05:13,367
You didn't tell anyone else,
did you?

100
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:15,033
Of course not.

101
00:05:15,167 --> 00:05:16,333
And you?

102
00:05:16,467 --> 00:05:17,800
Of course not either.

103
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:29,733
Why did you delete it?

104
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:34,133
This only brings a problem.

105
00:05:34,833 --> 00:05:37,433
There's already a lot going on
in my life, in my family,

106
00:05:37,567 --> 00:05:38,700
this also adds to it.

107
00:05:45,267 --> 00:05:48,567
All the cargo units,
sealed and tagged, Boss.

108
00:05:48,867 --> 00:05:52,033
The ETA is less than 48 hours.

109
00:05:52,167 --> 00:05:55,033
All the plate numbers are fake.

110
00:05:55,700 --> 00:05:58,300
And all the escorts
are paid for too.

111
00:05:58,433 --> 00:06:02,300
That's a whopping 500 million
dollar drug shipment.

112
00:06:03,033 --> 00:06:05,000
We can't afford another fiasco.

113
00:06:05,133 --> 00:06:07,200
We lost too much already.

114
00:06:08,733 --> 00:06:09,533
Exactly.

115
00:06:10,567 --> 00:06:12,067
That's what I told Matias.

116
00:06:12,967 --> 00:06:14,433
No checkpoints.

117
00:06:14,567 --> 00:06:16,167
No leaks.

118
00:06:16,733 --> 00:06:19,333
I've also changed the routes
of our supply chain.

119
00:06:22,100 --> 00:06:23,467
That easy?

120
00:06:24,400 --> 00:06:26,967
Customs and coast guards
have tightened up

121
00:06:27,100 --> 00:06:29,700
after our shipment was busted.

122
00:06:29,833 --> 00:06:31,267
How'd you do it?

123
00:06:34,433 --> 00:06:35,467
Okay.

124
00:06:36,167 --> 00:06:37,167
I get it.

125
00:06:38,200 --> 00:06:40,033
You have networks.

126
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:42,067
That's why I partnered with you.

127
00:06:42,700 --> 00:06:45,167
But what if there's
a smart-aleck again?

128
00:06:46,433 --> 00:06:47,633
What's that name?

129
00:06:47,767 --> 00:06:49,900
Officer Miguel Delgado?

130
00:06:50,033 --> 00:06:52,267
He's not our problem anymore.

131
00:06:52,700 --> 00:06:54,567
He's in stitches
over Ramon's death.

132
00:06:56,033 --> 00:06:59,233
I'm sure he's already been
implicated in the investigation.

133
00:06:59,367 --> 00:07:01,467
Parak is focused on him.

134
00:07:25,133 --> 00:07:26,867
Joey, who are you looking
at there?

135
00:07:28,133 --> 00:07:29,600
Are you waiting for someone?

136
00:07:32,800 --> 00:07:34,033
Nothing, Mother.

137
00:07:42,167 --> 00:07:46,800
Are you thinking if your father
will visit us?

138
00:07:47,433 --> 00:07:48,667
Sorry, Joey.

139
00:07:49,100 --> 00:07:51,767
I can't really forgive him yet.

140
00:07:51,900 --> 00:07:54,367
I can't face him yet.

141
00:07:54,500 --> 00:07:59,567
But that doesn't mean you have
to feel the same way.

142
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:04,400
Whatever your father's
shortcomings and sins...

143
00:08:05,933 --> 00:08:07,367
that's only on me.

144
00:08:08,767 --> 00:08:10,600
You don't have to carry that.

145
00:08:11,167 --> 00:08:13,967
I also know that you miss
your father so much.

146
00:08:14,767 --> 00:08:18,733
So if you want to check
on him...

147
00:08:19,900 --> 00:08:21,800
meet and talk to him...

148
00:08:23,233 --> 00:08:24,800
I won't stop you.

149
00:08:33,267 --> 00:08:34,967
But please, Joey...

150
00:08:36,867 --> 00:08:40,167
don't force me to make peace
with him either.

151
00:08:42,067 --> 00:08:43,667
I can't do it yet.

152
00:08:46,167 --> 00:08:47,333
Yes, Mother.

153
00:09:20,033 --> 00:09:21,533
- Give me!
- It's not possible, Ma'am.

154
00:09:21,667 --> 00:09:23,333
Give me the medicine.

155
00:09:23,467 --> 00:09:25,433
Ma'am...

156
00:09:25,567 --> 00:09:27,000
Give me that!

157
00:09:27,133 --> 00:09:30,067
Get out of here!

158
00:09:30,233 --> 00:09:33,367
Give me my medicine!
I'm in pain!

159
00:09:33,500 --> 00:09:35,900
- Mom! Mom!
- Andrew, Andrew, please.

160
00:09:36,033 --> 00:09:38,567
Please, Andrew.
Give me, give me.

161
00:09:38,700 --> 00:09:40,700
She doesn't want to give me
my medicine.

162
00:09:40,833 --> 00:09:42,833
She doesn't want to give it.
She's being greedy.

163
00:09:42,967 --> 00:09:43,767
Give me.

164
00:09:43,900 --> 00:09:46,000
Maybe we can increase
my mom's dosage

165
00:09:46,133 --> 00:09:47,533
because she's already
in so much pain. You see.

166
00:09:47,667 --> 00:09:49,000
Andrew, no!

167
00:09:51,400 --> 00:09:54,300
If we give her more,
she'll overdose.

168
00:09:54,567 --> 00:09:55,633
So be it!

169
00:09:56,400 --> 00:10:00,733
I'd rather die to end
this suffering!

170
00:10:01,833 --> 00:10:03,100
Get out of this room

171
00:10:03,233 --> 00:10:04,800
if you don't want to give me
my medicine.

172
00:10:04,933 --> 00:10:06,033
Get out!

173
00:10:07,967 --> 00:10:10,800
Get out! You, especially you!
Get out of here!

174
00:10:10,933 --> 00:10:12,933
Get out! Get out...

175
00:10:13,067 --> 00:10:16,533
Andrew, make her leave.
Get her out of here!

176
00:10:25,433 --> 00:10:26,700
Andrew...

177
00:10:37,700 --> 00:10:40,200
There are days she's
just like that.

178
00:10:40,700 --> 00:10:42,367
Needing more meds.

179
00:10:46,233 --> 00:10:50,033
Maybe we can talk to the doctor
to increase mom's dosage?

180
00:10:50,333 --> 00:10:54,200
Andrew, mom's dosage
is already high.

181
00:10:54,333 --> 00:10:55,567
But she's still in pain.

182
00:10:55,700 --> 00:10:57,267
She's always in pain.

183
00:10:58,333 --> 00:10:59,833
Remember what the doctor said?

184
00:10:59,967 --> 00:11:03,833
That's why we're managing
her meds as best we can.

185
00:11:03,967 --> 00:11:08,967
But her painkillers
are wearing off quickly.

186
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:13,867
Anyway, have you eaten yet?

187
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,967
I'll ask our nanny to prepare
something for you, okay?

188
00:11:18,333 --> 00:11:19,367
Wait here.

189
00:11:21,867 --> 00:11:24,533
Yes, we received the payment.

190
00:11:24,967 --> 00:11:25,767
Thank you again.

191
00:11:25,900 --> 00:11:27,867
It's really nice doing business
with you.

192
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,333
Until next time.

193
00:11:32,067 --> 00:11:33,333
Is that Mr. Lee?

194
00:11:37,067 --> 00:11:37,933
Yes.

195
00:11:38,867 --> 00:11:41,567
The shipment landed,
and he's thrilled.

196
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:44,600
He also said that our items
are top-tier quality.

197
00:11:44,733 --> 00:11:46,033
And guess what?

198
00:11:46,167 --> 00:11:48,133
He wants exclusivity.

199
00:11:48,267 --> 00:11:49,200
Great.

200
00:11:49,333 --> 00:11:52,600
So that means the next price
will be higher.

201
00:11:54,867 --> 00:11:56,267
We have another piece
of good news.

202
00:11:57,067 --> 00:11:59,200
We didn't just silenced Delgado.

203
00:12:00,400 --> 00:12:03,067
He's still the number one
suspect in Ramon's death.

204
00:12:05,067 --> 00:12:07,267
Poor Delgado.

205
00:12:07,400 --> 00:12:10,300
A fall guy and a scapegoat.

206
00:12:10,433 --> 00:12:13,933
The stars are finally aligning
in favor of us again.

207
00:12:14,867 --> 00:12:16,133
Speaking of Ramon,

208
00:12:17,233 --> 00:12:19,933
does Loloy have an update
on what I'm looking for?

209
00:12:26,833 --> 00:12:30,567
<i> Vote straight, Kalasag Party!</i>

210
00:12:30,700 --> 00:12:33,267
<i> Zoom in. Close up, that's all.</i>

211
00:12:37,300 --> 00:12:38,633
<i> It's so boring.</i>

212
00:12:39,933 --> 00:12:41,700
<i> What's with you?</i>

213
00:12:41,833 --> 00:12:44,500
<i>Didn't you agree to be
my assistant</i>

214
00:12:44,633 --> 00:12:46,233
<i> so you could make money?</i>

215
00:12:46,367 --> 00:12:50,633
<i>You know, Andrew, instead
of complaining all the time,</i>

216
00:12:50,800 --> 00:12:55,300
<i>just watch what I do
so you can learn something.</i>

217
00:13:00,200 --> 00:13:02,100
<i> Where are you going?</i>

218
00:13:02,233 --> 00:13:04,233
<i> I'll just go to the CR.</i>

219
00:13:04,367 --> 00:13:06,100
<i> Go, go, go, go.</i>

220
00:13:25,567 --> 00:13:27,167
<i> Mom! Mom...</i>

221
00:13:30,033 --> 00:13:32,500
<i> Andrew!</i>

222
00:13:32,633 --> 00:13:33,733
<i> Mom!</i>

223
00:13:45,467 --> 00:13:46,300
<i> Mom.</i>

224
00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:50,500
<i>- Son.
- Mom.</i>

225
00:14:02,633 --> 00:14:03,967
<i> Help!</i>

226
00:14:10,533 --> 00:14:12,200
<i> Mr. Dizon,</i>

227
00:14:12,633 --> 00:14:14,433
<i> Ma'am, good morning.</i>

228
00:14:14,967 --> 00:14:16,700
<i>The Special Investigations
Unit's initial report</i>

229
00:14:16,833 --> 00:14:18,100
<i> is complete.</i>

230
00:14:18,233 --> 00:14:21,733
<i>And based on the available
forensic and ballistic analysis,</i>

231
00:14:22,033 --> 00:14:23,933
<i>your mother was not the primary
target.</i>

232
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:26,800
<i>She was one of the several
casualties during the crossfire.</i>

233
00:14:26,933 --> 00:14:28,933
<i>Don't tell me it was a crossfire</i>

234
00:14:29,100 --> 00:14:30,733
<i>because there was no shooting
around her.</i>

235
00:14:30,867 --> 00:14:31,800
<i> That was not a stray bullet.</i>

236
00:14:31,933 --> 00:14:33,667
<i>The intention was to shoot
my mom.</i>

237
00:14:33,800 --> 00:14:36,600
<i>We reviewed the CCTV
and crowd footage.</i>

238
00:14:36,933 --> 00:14:39,533
<i>We did not see a clear angle
of the shooter.</i>

239
00:14:39,900 --> 00:14:40,967
<i> The slug that was recovered</i>

240
00:14:41,100 --> 00:14:43,567
<i>did not match the gun we found
at the site.</i>

241
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:46,933
<i>And there is also no witness who
can corroborate your statement</i>

242
00:14:47,233 --> 00:14:49,233
<i>that your mother was
specifically targeted.</i>

243
00:14:49,567 --> 00:14:52,200
<i>You're closing a case
based on lack of evidence</i>

244
00:14:52,333 --> 00:14:55,800
<i>while my mom is in the hospital,
dying right now.</i>

245
00:14:55,933 --> 00:14:58,300
<i>I understand your frustrations,
Mr. Dizon.</i>

246
00:14:58,633 --> 00:15:01,533
<i>But unless we get a new evidence
or a witness</i>

247
00:15:01,700 --> 00:15:03,500
<i>who can testify
to your statement,</i>

248
00:15:03,633 --> 00:15:05,100
<i> the case will remain closed.</i>

249
00:15:05,233 --> 00:15:07,400
<i>The official ruling
is collateral fatality.</i>

250
00:15:07,533 --> 00:15:09,200
<i> Useless police officers!</i>

251
00:15:09,333 --> 00:15:12,400
<i>Just say that you're covering up
for someone.</i>

252
00:15:12,533 --> 00:15:15,667
<i> This is a cover-up.</i>

253
00:15:15,800 --> 00:15:18,733
<i>It's easy for you to say
that my father is a bad person!</i>

254
00:15:18,867 --> 00:15:20,133
<i>Because you're mad
at the police!</i>

255
00:15:20,267 --> 00:15:21,633
<i> You're the one who's biased!</i>

256
00:15:25,833 --> 00:15:28,400
They've traced the CCTV
in the office.

257
00:15:28,967 --> 00:15:32,900
Just a little patience,
we'll track down that woman too.

258
00:15:33,767 --> 00:15:34,767
Very good.

259
00:15:37,267 --> 00:15:39,767
I can't wait to meet her
face-to-face...

260
00:15:41,433 --> 00:15:43,600
so that I'll be the one
filming her

261
00:15:44,133 --> 00:15:45,767
while she's crying,

262
00:15:45,900 --> 00:15:49,333
scared, and begging.

263
00:15:50,867 --> 00:15:53,767
Because she made a mistake
with whom she messed up with.

264
00:16:16,933 --> 00:16:19,167
Relax, Joey.
You're getting paranoid.

265
00:16:34,333 --> 00:16:36,033
Joey Delgado, Ma'am?

266
00:16:36,167 --> 00:16:37,100
Yes.

267
00:16:37,233 --> 00:16:38,567
Let's go.

268
00:16:57,800 --> 00:17:01,700
Well, there's another scenario.
We were all stuck in the mud,

269
00:17:01,833 --> 00:17:05,800
then, after our training,
we took a shower together.

270
00:17:05,933 --> 00:17:07,433
Then, there was someone else
with us.

271
00:17:07,567 --> 00:17:08,967
Do you remember Herera?

272
00:17:09,533 --> 00:17:11,900
- Herera, yes.
- I remember him.

273
00:17:12,033 --> 00:17:13,100
What was he wearing?

274
00:17:13,900 --> 00:17:14,733
Not a brief.

275
00:17:14,900 --> 00:17:16,067
Panty!

276
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:20,500
The life of a suspended officer
is pretty good, isn't it?

277
00:17:21,233 --> 00:17:24,233
Just laughing and drinking.

278
00:17:24,367 --> 00:17:28,367
Instead of fixing the problem,
he's getting wasted!

279
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:34,000
Maybe what they're accusing him
of is true.

280
00:17:34,133 --> 00:17:35,667
Who do you think he is, a saint?

281
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:38,133
When he is hiding so many sins.

282
00:17:42,233 --> 00:17:42,967
Buddy...

283
00:17:43,100 --> 00:17:43,800
He wants to fight.

284
00:17:43,933 --> 00:17:44,667
Look, he stood up.

285
00:17:44,800 --> 00:17:46,700
Don't.

286
00:17:46,833 --> 00:17:48,100
Don't pay attention.

287
00:17:48,267 --> 00:17:50,267
Ignore them, Bro.

288
00:17:50,400 --> 00:17:51,500
Let's just continue chatting.

289
00:17:51,633 --> 00:17:52,933
Let's go!

290
00:17:53,067 --> 00:17:53,800
Waiter!

291
00:17:59,867 --> 00:18:00,700
Who's that?

292
00:18:07,267 --> 00:18:08,933
Isn't that Boss Idol?

293
00:18:09,067 --> 00:18:10,333
The one in Ka-Tirada.

294
00:18:10,467 --> 00:18:12,367
- Yes, that's him.
- Isn't that him?

295
00:18:12,500 --> 00:18:13,700
That's him.

296
00:18:13,833 --> 00:18:15,333
That's him, isn't it?

297
00:18:15,467 --> 00:18:16,433
Boss Idol.

298
00:18:16,567 --> 00:18:17,533
Yes.

299
00:18:35,667 --> 00:18:37,300
My condolences.

300
00:18:37,433 --> 00:18:38,367
Thank you.

301
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:40,833
How did you meet my husband?

302
00:18:42,567 --> 00:18:44,467
We don't know each
other personally.

303
00:18:44,867 --> 00:18:48,067
Actually, I'm here for you.

304
00:18:50,633 --> 00:18:52,367
Okay, Mother,
I'm on my way home.

305
00:18:54,133 --> 00:18:55,567
Take care. I love you!

306
00:19:15,100 --> 00:19:16,700
Sir, can you hurry up, please?

307
00:19:17,633 --> 00:19:18,567
Why?

308
00:19:21,800 --> 00:19:23,067
Just hurry up, Sir.

309
00:19:23,200 --> 00:19:25,300
My mother needs me.

310
00:19:25,433 --> 00:19:26,267
Okay.

311
00:19:26,400 --> 00:19:28,233
My husband is kind.

312
00:19:28,400 --> 00:19:30,133
But we have four children.

313
00:19:30,267 --> 00:19:32,567
Life is very hard.

314
00:19:33,500 --> 00:19:38,133
His meager salary can no
longer support our family.

315
00:19:38,267 --> 00:19:40,333
But sometimes, I was surprised.

316
00:19:40,467 --> 00:19:43,400
He had a lot of money
and I made him confess.

317
00:19:44,433 --> 00:19:46,267
He also couldn't hide it.

318
00:19:46,833 --> 00:19:50,300
He admitted that he was
doing some illegal things.

319
00:19:50,433 --> 00:19:52,833
Sir, at the next corner,
turn right.

320
00:19:55,233 --> 00:19:57,500
Ma'am, that will
be a longer route.

321
00:19:57,633 --> 00:19:58,833
It's okay.

322
00:19:58,967 --> 00:20:01,233
I need to buy medicine
for my mother.

323
00:20:01,400 --> 00:20:03,067
I'll just add a tip for you.

324
00:20:04,667 --> 00:20:05,567
Okay, it's up to you.

325
00:20:06,767 --> 00:20:08,267
Just hurry up, please, Sir.

326
00:20:09,600 --> 00:20:14,900
I stopped him several times,
but he said it was safe.

327
00:20:15,933 --> 00:20:20,533
Until one day, he looked
so scared when he got home.

328
00:20:20,667 --> 00:20:22,767
He said he had to hide.

329
00:20:23,767 --> 00:20:25,967
I said, let's go get help.

330
00:20:26,967 --> 00:20:29,967
Well, if he had just told
the truth but he said he can't

331
00:20:30,100 --> 00:20:31,833
because Parak would kill him.

332
00:20:35,433 --> 00:20:36,300
Parak?

333
00:20:39,533 --> 00:20:41,533
Is Miguel Delgado the
one he was referring to?

334
00:20:41,667 --> 00:20:44,133
I'm not sure who he was
referring to,

335
00:20:44,267 --> 00:20:47,067
but I'm sure
it wasn't Major Delgado.

336
00:20:47,967 --> 00:20:50,000
Because the day Ramon
disappeared,

337
00:20:50,133 --> 00:20:51,900
he left something with me.

338
00:20:52,033 --> 00:20:55,333
He said, if anything bad
happens to him,

339
00:20:55,467 --> 00:20:58,200
I'll give it to Miguel Delgado.

340
00:21:02,733 --> 00:21:04,667
We've got a lot of people
with us.

341
00:21:05,867 --> 00:21:07,800
What a poor guy!

342
00:21:08,567 --> 00:21:10,900
He's sulking!

343
00:21:11,033 --> 00:21:13,767
That's because his family
left him!

344
00:21:14,833 --> 00:21:18,300
Because what he did
was shameful!

345
00:21:18,433 --> 00:21:19,633
He deserves that!

346
00:21:27,500 --> 00:21:28,267
What did you say?

347
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:29,500
Bro, ignore them.

348
00:21:30,933 --> 00:21:32,167
It's true!

349
00:21:32,300 --> 00:21:34,667
Didn't your wife and daughter
leave you?

350
00:21:35,833 --> 00:21:37,067
You don't have a career anymore!

351
00:21:37,200 --> 00:21:38,067
You don't have a family anymore!

352
00:21:38,767 --> 00:21:39,700
Do you know what you're called?

353
00:21:40,967 --> 00:21:41,867
Loser!

354
00:21:49,867 --> 00:21:50,833
Enough, Bro! Enough!

355
00:21:50,967 --> 00:21:52,567
Dude, enough! Enough!

356
00:21:54,867 --> 00:21:56,733
Dude, enough!

357
00:21:59,333 --> 00:22:00,333
Enough!

358
00:22:03,333 --> 00:22:04,500
That's enough!

359
00:22:04,633 --> 00:22:05,733
Enough, Bro!

360
00:22:23,200 --> 00:22:24,533
Who's the loser now?

361
00:22:34,500 --> 00:22:35,433
Thank you.

362
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:45,900
Mother.

363
00:22:46,033 --> 00:22:47,467
Joey, why are you home late?

364
00:22:48,667 --> 00:22:49,933
I just passed by somewhere.

365
00:22:51,433 --> 00:22:53,233
I'm sure you're hungry.

366
00:22:53,367 --> 00:22:54,600
- Right?
- Yes.

367
00:22:54,733 --> 00:22:56,333
Come on, come on.

368
00:22:58,633 --> 00:23:00,900
Perfect timing,
I'm done cooking.

369
00:23:34,800 --> 00:23:37,733
Metropolitan State University.

370
00:23:37,867 --> 00:23:38,900
That's the video you took.

371
00:23:39,033 --> 00:23:40,367
It's wrong to delete that video.

372
00:23:40,500 --> 00:23:41,267
I'll take care of this.

373
00:23:41,400 --> 00:23:43,467
Why do you need to install CCTV?

374
00:23:43,600 --> 00:23:46,167
We need to make sure Joey
doesn't have a stalker.

375
00:23:46,300 --> 00:23:48,667
What if someone gets
into this house?

376
00:23:48,800 --> 00:23:52,067
What if someone tries
to kill me again, Andrew?

377
00:23:52,200 --> 00:23:54,333
Do you know my daughter,
Joey Delgado?

378
00:23:54,467 --> 00:23:56,033
She went to the market.

379
00:23:56,200 --> 00:23:57,400
Who are you?

380
00:23:57,533 --> 00:24:00,100
Jay's Pro Gym. JPG?

381
00:24:00,233 --> 00:24:01,033
- Sorry.
- It's okay.

382
00:24:01,167 --> 00:24:02,867
Did you see a woman
in a red jacket?

383
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:04,400
My sister ran away from me.

384
00:24:04,533 --> 00:24:05,400
Boss, he's here.

385
00:24:05,533 --> 00:24:06,500
Good job, Parak.

386
00:24:06,633 --> 00:24:08,233
What do you need from
the woman you're after?

387
00:24:08,367 --> 00:24:09,700
Hey! Get in the car!

388
00:24:09,833 --> 00:24:11,700
Your husband is a suspect
in the death

389
00:24:11,833 --> 00:24:13,400
of Staff Sergeant Ramon Orbos.

390
00:24:13,533 --> 00:24:14,800
I have evidence!

391
00:24:14,933 --> 00:24:16,567
You can't take my father.

392
00:24:16,700 --> 00:24:19,967
It's time to meet that freaking
girl and get that video.
